// The photo site's Pages configuration (CLAUDE.md, The photo site, item 5).
//
// Pages reads this file from the project's root directory, photos/, on every
// build, and the dashboard then shows these bindings read-only. What this file
// cannot hold (build command, root directory, watch paths, custom domain,
// branch controls, preview access policy, fail mode) is in README.md's hosting
// table, which is the only other copy.
//
// Three rules, each from item 5:
//   - env.preview and env.production each restate EVERY key below, because
//     overriding one non-inheritable key in an environment means restating
//     them all.
//   - The top level names the PREVIEW resources. Anything that matches no
//     environment then falls back to preview storage, never to production.
//     wrangler pages dev uses the top level, with local stand-ins for both.
//   - Every database_id is written out, and no secret goes in this file or
//     anywhere in the tree. Secrets are Pages secrets, named in README.md.
//
// The admin guard (#151, lib/access.js) read two vars here. Neither is
// secret: every Access token carries both. Since #224 the admin guard is the
// site's own admin session (lib/admin-session.js), and only the coach guard
// below reads ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN. ACCESS_AUD is read by nothing: it stays as
// the record of the admin application's tag until #226 removes the
// application, and with it this var.
//   - ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN is the Zero Trust team's domain: the tokens' issuer,
//     and where the signing keys are fetched from.
//   - ACCESS_AUD is the AUD tag of the Access application that signs this
//     environment's requests. Preview deployments sit behind the project's
//     Pages preview application, production behind the admin application on
//     photos.madcowsailing.com, so the two differ. A tag changes only if its
//     application is deleted and recreated.
// The admins' addresses were the third thing it read, the ADMIN_EMAILS
// secret, which nothing reads since #224 either.
//
// The coach guard (#192) reads the same team domain and one more var:
//   - ACCESS_COACH_AUD is the AUD tag of the application that signs /coach:
//     the coach application on photos.madcowsailing.com in production, and
//     the Pages preview application on a preview, which signs every path, so
//     there it equals ACCESS_AUD.
// The coaches' addresses are the COACH_EMAILS secret.
//
// The request form at /ask (#220) reads one more var:
//   - TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is the site key of the Turnstile widget
//     "madcowphotos ask", which serves photos.madcowsailing.com and
//     madcowphotos.pages.dev, so both environments name the same one. It is
//     public: every /ask page carries it. Its secret is the
//     TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY secret. Locally, photos/.dev.vars sets Cloudflare's
//     test keys in place of both (README, Running it locally).
//
// photos/test/config.test.mjs holds these rules, and it fails if preview and
// production ever share a database or a bucket.
//
// nodejs_compat (#218): lib/password.js imports scrypt from node:crypto, the
// runtime's own, since Workers has no Argon2id and caps PBKDF2 below OWASP's
// count (CLAUDE.md, The photo site, item 23). A compatibility_date of
// 2026-08-04 or later turns the flag on by default, and Cloudflare's crypto
// page says a project need not remove it. It is named anyway: photos/package.json
// installs nothing, so Pages builds the Functions with the wrangler in its own
// build image, not the one pinned in the repo root, and a build that did not
// know the dated default would fail to resolve the import.
{
  "name": "madcowphotos",
  "pages_build_output_dir": "./public",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-25",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],

  "vars": {
    "SITE_ENV": "preview",
    "ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN": "https://madcowsailing.cloudflareaccess.com",
    "ACCESS_AUD": "da25aceb2d1232a48684240aed72446c70a829ca0f71e8a93c2041f50f3f4700",
    "ACCESS_COACH_AUD": "da25aceb2d1232a48684240aed72446c70a829ca0f71e8a93c2041f50f3f4700",
    "TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY": "0x4AAAAAAFO0znmMP-mkXRR5"
  },
  "d1_databases": [
    {
      "binding": "DB",
      "database_name": "madcowphotos-preview",
      "database_id": "1cf98564-46b0-4e84-b015-2aa6767c1f2a",
      "migrations_dir": "migrations"
    }
  ],
  "r2_buckets": [
    { "binding": "MEDIA", "bucket_name": "madcowphotos-preview" }
  ],

  "env": {
    "preview": {
      "vars": {
        "SITE_ENV": "preview",
        "ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN": "https://madcowsailing.cloudflareaccess.com",
        "ACCESS_AUD": "da25aceb2d1232a48684240aed72446c70a829ca0f71e8a93c2041f50f3f4700",
        "ACCESS_COACH_AUD": "da25aceb2d1232a48684240aed72446c70a829ca0f71e8a93c2041f50f3f4700",
        "TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY": "0x4AAAAAAFO0znmMP-mkXRR5"
      },
      "d1_databases": [
        {
          "binding": "DB",
          "database_name": "madcowphotos-preview",
          "database_id": "1cf98564-46b0-4e84-b015-2aa6767c1f2a",
          "migrations_dir": "migrations"
        }
      ],
      "r2_buckets": [
        { "binding": "MEDIA", "bucket_name": "madcowphotos-preview" }
      ]
    },
    "production": {
      "vars": {
        "SITE_ENV": "production",
        "ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN": "https://madcowsailing.cloudflareaccess.com",
        "ACCESS_AUD": "78d0a143ee4090db61bac7bf71d2d6a40055fcc1f99b6dfa82105175c33727f1",
        "ACCESS_COACH_AUD": "3be126b61281628beeb5a8674c84d1741c0c5582a3071e52cde925cb26314946",
        "TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY": "0x4AAAAAAFO0znmMP-mkXRR5"
      },
      "d1_databases": [
        {
          "binding": "DB",
          "database_name": "madcowphotos",
          "database_id": "ea7cb9f4-80f8-4cac-bbf1-a2b09d476b15",
          "migrations_dir": "migrations"
        }
      ],
      "r2_buckets": [
        { "binding": "MEDIA", "bucket_name": "madcowphotos" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
